\index{L-packet}
\begin{defn}{L-packet}{l-packet}
Let \(\Pi\) be an irreducible smooth \(K\)-representation of \(G\). Then the set \(L(\Pi)\) of isomorphism classes
of irreducible components of the restriction \(\Pi|_{G'}\) is called an \emph{L-packet}.
\end{defn}

We classify the irreducible smooth \(K\)-representations of \(G'\) by these L-packets.

\begin{prop}{Properties of L-packets: I}{propofL-packetsI}
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item If \(\Pi\) is an irreducible smooth \(K\)-representation of \(G\) the restriction of \(\Pi\) to \(G'\)
    is semisimple of finite length and multiplicity 1.
    \item  Any irreducible smooth \(K\)-representation of \(G'\) belongs to a unique \(L\)-packet.

    \item For two irreducible smooth \(K\)-representations \(\Pi_1, \Pi_2\) of \(G\),
  \[
    L(\Pi_1) = L(\Pi_2) \iff \Pi_1 = (\chi \circ \det) \otimes \Pi_2
  \]

  \end{enumerate}
  Note that the trivial character of \(G'\) is the unique finite-dimensional irreducible smooth
  \(K\)-representation of \(G'\), it is degenerate and forms an \(L\)-packet \(L(1) = L(\chi \circ \det)\) for
  any smooth \(K\)-character \(\chi\) of \(F^*\). for some \(K\)-character \(\chi \circ \det\) of \(G\).
\end{prop}

\begin{Proof}
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item By~\cref{th:3.2}, taking the natural inclusion $f: \underline{H} \to \underline{G}$, since $G/H$ is compact
      the restriction $\Pi|_H$ is semisimple of finite length. Since $Z$ acts by a scalar character in any
      irreducible representation $\Pi$ (as $K$ is algebraically closed), the restriction from $H$ to $G'$ does
      not change the reducibility or the of subrepresentations (it only forgets the central character). Therefore, $\Pi|_{G'}$ is semisimple of finite length.

      For multiplicity, \cref{lm:lem3} states that if a functor $\text{Hom}_U(-, \theta)$ is exact and $\dim
      \text{Hom}_U(\Pi, \theta) = 1$, then $\Pi|_H$ has multiplicity 1. Let $U$ be the subgroup of unipotent
      upper triangular matrices and $\theta$ be a non-degenerate character of $U$ (see~\cref{df:whittakerSp}). By the
      uniqueness of Whittaker models for $GL_2(F)$, for any infinite-dimensional irreducible representation
      $\Pi$, we have $\dim_R \mathcal{W}_Y(\Pi) = 1$ (which is isomorphic to $\text{Hom}_U(\Pi, \theta)$).
      By~\cref{lm:lem3}, the restriction $\Pi|_{G'}$ is multiplicity 1. (Note: Finite-dimensional representations are
      characters $\chi \circ \det$, which are trivial on $G'$, hence the restriction is the trivial
